From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dreyk <dreyksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] https-dns-proxy: update to 2026.10.19

While the upstream connection is down, both proxies exit about every
4-9 s with

  [F] dns_poller.c:39 c-ares needed more IO event handler, than the
  number of provided nameservers: 2

and procd restarts them until the connection is back. The poller
allocated one libev watcher per bootstrap server and gave up when
c-ares opened more sockets than that, which it does while its queries
fail. 63c49b4 ("Fix bootstrap socket watcher exhaustion") allocates the
watchers on demand.

The update also brings, among others:
- b4dd4d4 https_client: allocate socket watchers on demand
- 1fa4e76 https_client: bound in-flight requests
- 4923f8f https_client: recover from receive errors
- dd5f52a Fix resolver list getting stuck after a partial bootstrap result
- 83f6b72 dns_tcp: prevent frame length overflow
- c437451 Bind HTTPS and bootstrap DNS sockets to an outbound interface
  (new option -I, not used by the service)

The options the service passes are unchanged; with -u and -g both set
the group handling of 2746cdd and 055e3a7 does not apply.

Seen on an OpenWrt 25.12 router (aarch64) with a PPPoE uplink that
forwarded no IP traffic for 7 minutes: 50 exits of the old version in
3.5 minutes. The new version builds without new dependencies and serves
DNS over HTTPS on both default instances.
---
 net/https-dns-proxy/Makefile | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/https-dns-proxy/Makefile b/net/https-dns-proxy/Makefile
--- a/net/https-dns-proxy/Makefile
+++ b/net/https-dns-proxy/Makefile
@@ -2,14 +2,14 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=https-dns-proxy
-PKG_VERSION:=2026.05.06
-PKG_RELEASE:=2
+PKG_VERSION:=2026.10.19
+PKG_RELEASE:=1
 PKG_CPE_ID:=cpe:/a:mossdef:https-dns-proxy
 
